NAME
     su - become another user

SYNOPSIS
     su [-] [-c COMMAND] [USER]

DESCRIPTION
     su starts a shell as USER (root by default), asking for that user's
     password unless the caller is already root.

OPTIONS
     -           a login shell: the environment and directory are that
                 user's, as though they had logged in
     -c COMMAND  run COMMAND instead of an interactive shell

SEE ALSO
     sudo(1), login(1), id(1)
